WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.230 align:start position:0%
 
earlier today i received orders from my  superior i'm being sent to investigate a  mysterious scp located under a warehouse  on the outskirts of london it seems  important as the scp was just discovered  and the overseer council wants a  detailed report on it right away i pull  up outside of the port superior canning  company warehouse it is abandoned and  from the look of it has been for a long  time i enter the building and make my  way to an opening at the far side of the  warehouse i descend the narrow stairwell  where i see a small black door i was  told there was always a guard posted by  the door there was no one here i stop  just outside of the black door and look  up above the door handle is a placard  that says scp foundation department of  abnormalities i'm in the right place but  nothing feels right maybe i should just  turn around and tell my superior i  couldn't find the door i take a deep  breath grab the handle and turn the door  doesn't budge i step back for a moment  and take a breath of relief then i  glance to the side of the door and see  the sliding lock my stomach sinks i move  the metal rod aside and try the door  again this time it swings open i shake  my head and dismay and walk into the  other side of the black door i have now  entered scp-3790  a series of dim emergency lights flicker  on there are four doors on the other  side of the hallway is an elevator  hello i'd say only slightly louder than  a whisper there is no response i walk  along the grated floor the metal rattles  under my boots i can see through the  grating and it appears there are several  floors below me i come to the first door  and examine it all of the doors are  identical they are made up of heavy  metal a sliding panel that covers a  glass viewport and placards that  identify what is in the room all of the  handles to the doors have been broken  off and the doors themselves have been  welded shut it seems that whoever  abandoned the department of  abnormalities wanted to make sure  whatever is in these rooms never got out  as i stare into the room i begin to feel  something well up inside of me i zone  out for a moment when i regain my  bearings my hand has moved itself to the  spot where the door handle once was as  if while i was in my days something  tried to trick me into opening the door  i immediately shove my hands into my  pockets turn and walk back toward the  black door to get out of this place  something is not right here as i  approach the exit the door slams shut i  race over to it and try turning the knob  it will not budge i've been locked in  scp-3790  i begin to panic as my eyes start from  door to door scanning for a way out  there is nowhere to go but deeper into  the department of abnormalities i glance  down to my right and notice something  lying on the ground it's a clipboard i  pick it up and skim through the pages of  the legal pad that is attached to it  most of what is written seems like the  ravings of a madman but on one page  there are some coherent notes it says  think it's about time need to lock down  the other sides before i go take care  there is a list of 10 roman numerals  with either the word locked or unlocked  beside them  7 8  and 10 all remain unlocked i'm not sure  if this is a good or a bad thing but it  seems that whoever was here before me is  now on their way to complete what they  started i tossed the clipboard and  looked down the corridor hoping that a  magical door will appear and let me out  of the department of abnormalities after  several minutes i decide to explore  scp-3790 more thoroughly perhaps there  is another way out on a different level  this gets my hopes up slightly but part  of me believes that this will be where i  spend the rest of my short life i walk  back up to the door where i think i hear  music coming from i wipe the dust and  grime off the placard and read what it  says the name written on it is vivaldi i  slide the panel away from the viewport  and look inside the chamber is  completely empty except for one object  in the far corner of the room a violin  is propped up against the wall in front  of it is a broken bow i squint my eyes  to get a better look at the instrument  it seems normal enough suddenly an  uneasy feeling comes over me like i'm  being watched i whip the panel closed  over the viewport and back away from the  door i turn down the hallway and walk to  the next door the name on the placard  for this room is montezuma's face i'm a  little hesitant to open the panel and  peer inside because of what might be  looking back at me i take a breath to  build a bit of courage and go for it i  slide the panel open and to my relief  all that is on the other side of the  viewport is an empty room with a metal  table in the center on it rests in  ornate wooden chest the chest has been  secured with a large steel padlock i put  my face a little closer to the glass to  try to get a better look at the markings  on the chest i can hear a faint clicking  sound like that of a ticking clock  coming from the room other than that all  is still i shrug and check the next door  to my surprise the next room has had its  placard removed when i peer into the  viewport the room is completely empty  this is strange as this door has also  been welded shut the fourth door in the  corridor has had its placard damaged  making the text on it unreadable i slide  the panel open and look inside there  appears to be nothing there but upon  closer inspection i see that the  concrete walls are covered in claw marks  it looks like whatever was in this  chamber had incredibly sharp talons and  was not happy about being detained on  the floor are pieces of bone that have  had the meat picked clean from them each  room is another mystery but offers no  way out of the department of  abnormalities my only hope is to go  deeper into the facility i push the  button for the elevator the door chimes  and slides open i step inside and look  at the seven buttons on the panel next  to each one is the level number it  corresponds to naturally i'm hesitant to  push any of them but i know i've got to  start somewhere if i'm going to have any  chance of getting out of here i reach  out and press the button for level two  the doors slide shut and the elevator  descends deeper into the depths of the  department of abnormalities the elevator  comes to a stop and the doors slide open  i step out into another corridor it  seems identical to the first one except  there is no black door on the opposite  side of the hallway this worries me a  little but i continue on according to  the placard of the first door of level 2  the room contains a man named ian i  slide the panel open and look through  the viewport in the corner of the room  sits a thin pale man wearing a dirty  straitjacket he is blindfolded and does  not seem to notice me his chest moves  slowly up and down i feel bad for the  man being cooped up in there all alone  but then again i have no idea what ian  is capable of the second room on this  level contains something called the  crying boy when i look into the chamber  i expect to see a young child weeping  instead there appears to be a painting  on an easel in the middle of the room it  has a sheet draped over it so i cannot  see what is on the canvas but from  inside the room i can hear the sobs of a  small child the placard for the third  room indicates that the creatures that  are contained within it are called the  watchers when i look into the chamber i  see three humanoid figures huddled  together they are all staring towards  the far corner with their backs turned  toward me the creatures sway back and  forth slowly it's an unsettling sight to  say the least one that will be difficult  to forget and will definitely haunt my  dreams the fourth door on level two has  no placard when i look inside i see  another dark hallway similar to the one  i'm in i try to force the door open as  it might be a way out but like all the  rest it has been welded shut i kick the  metal door hoping and wishfully thinking  it will make an impact but instead i  instantly regret my decision i  contemplate my extreme lack of karate  skills as i limp back to the elevator  and defeat i descend to the third level  room one on level three contains  something called the infinite cold when  i look into the chamber i can see that  the floor is covered with a thin layer  of ice what is odd is that the interior  of the room seems to go on forever in  all directions it even appears to extend  to the room next to it but when i look  into the viewport to the second room  there is a solid wall between the  infinite cold and the empty pedestal in  room two i checked the placard for the  second room and find that it is called  sorrow it looks like there was one  something on top of the pedestal but the  four finger marks left in the dust that  now covers it indicates the object had  been moved recently the third room is  named world without man unsurprisingly  the chamber is completely empty the  fourth room on this level is labeled  adam's hatred this does not seem like  something i want to see but i slide the  panel away from the viewport and glance  in anyway in the back of the room is a  large black mass slowly oscillating in  mid-air i feel anger begin to fill me  the rage of this creature is palpable  it's being transferred from the black  mass to me scared of what it or i might  do i run back to the elevator and hit  the button for level four on the placard  of the first room on level four are the  words the morning star all that is in  the chamber is a rusted sword hanging  from the wall however as i move my face  closer to the window to get a better  look the temperature starts to rise it  feels like the fires of hell are just on  the other side of this door the placard  for the next room is labeled wormwood  but when i open the panel to peer inside  there is something obstructing my view i  don't spend much time here and move on  to the next the placard on door 3 names  this anomaly as harmonia's necklace  within the chamber a golden chain hangs  from a post against the back wall a  single candle burns just beneath the  necklace illuminating the space around  it when i look closer at the candle i  realize the chamber has no floor the  light seems to be floating among  infinite darkness the fourth chamber on  this level has no placard when i look  inside the room is unlit all i feel is a  sense of dread a feeling that follows me  all the way back to the elevator i  descend to level 5. the first door is  labeled as the heart of man inside is a  human heart suspended in mid-air by a  wire hanging from the ceiling i look  closer and to my horror i see the heart  is still beating the entire room starts  to distort my own heart aches i run down  the hallway to the second door the  placard for this room has been pried off  the word hello has been scratched into  the metal where the label once was when  i try to slide the panel over to look  into the room i find that just like the  door itself the panel has also been  welded shut whatever is on the other  side of this door must truly be terrible  the third door contains something called  channel 55. in the room there is a small  crt television set under a dark cloth i  can see the light from the tv shining  through the sheet but cannot make out  the image on the screen the fourth door  of floor 5 has a placard with the words  living nightmare printed on it i pause  for a moment to think if i really want  to see what is inside this room i figure  i've come this far and maybe it's just a  trick to keep me from finding the exit i  slowly slide the panel away from the  viewport it makes a sound like a creaky  door opening in a haunted house in the  room there is a bed resting on a metal  frame someone appears to be lying on the  bed with a sheet pulled over their head  creepy i think i walk back to the  elevator and cannot help but feel i'm  about to reach something terrifyingly  significant in my journey one way or  another whatever is on the next two  floors will seal my fate i get off on  level six it looks identical to all the  previous floors the first room contains  something called mr silence resting on  the back chamber wall is a tall wooden  box it has been painted black with a  purple w adorning the front of it i hold  my breath for a moment it's so quiet  that the silence hurts my ears the  second room contains the dead man's  chair in the corner of the chamber is a  wooden seat there's no one sitting on it  but as i look at the shadow against the  wall there is clearly a figure seated  there i glanced back at the wooden chair  but it is still empty and upon a second  look at the shadow the figure is gone  the placard on the third door reads  let's see when i slide open the viewport  it is covered in ice i can't see  completely through the ice but from what  i can make out there seems to be a dark  shape standing in the middle of the room  the fourth door on level six contains  apollyon's crown there are scratch marks  all across the metal door it looks as if  something was trying to get into the  room instead of out of it in the chamber  itself is a silver lock box resting on a  table whatever is inside must be very  important to someone i enter the  elevator and press the button for level  seven the door slides shut and the  elevator begins to descend to the bottom  level i know that if there is no way out  on this floor i will be trapped like all  the other objects in the department of  abnormalities the bell chimes indicating  i've reached what i hope is my way out  of here the doors slide open i take a  few steps out into a corridor that looks  like all the rest i turn and gaze into  the first room on the floor instantly  terror fills every centimeter of space  in my core it feels as if my heart stops  frozen in fear for a moment i try to  scream but nothing escapes i come to my  senses and i'm able to use my legs again  i run back to the elevator and hit the  button for the first floor as the  elevator ascends back to where i began  this nightmarish tour my body trembles  more and more as soon as the elevator  chimes at level 1 without hesitation and  with my shaking hands and nimble fingers  i immediately rip open the button panel  and tear out the wires connected to  level seven no one should ever have to  see what is that far down in the  department of abnormalities and now no  one ever will now watch  scp-5545 mysterious tunnels in  antarctica abnormality or check out 25  most frightening scp

